# No Comments Unless Asked

Do not add comments to code unless the user explicitly asks for them.

## Rules

- Never write `//`, `///`, `/* */`, or `#` comments in new or edited code by default
- Do not add doc comments, section banners, or narrating comments
- Do not leave leftover comments explaining what changed
- Only add comments when the user explicitly requests them (e.g. "add comments", "document this")

```dart
// ❌ BAD — unsolicited comment
// Fetch animals from the API
final animals = await repository.fetchAnimals();

// ✅ GOOD — code only
final animals = await repository.fetchAnimals();
```

```dart
// ❌ BAD — narrating the change
// Fixed null check
if (animal != null) return animal.name;

// ✅ GOOD
if (animal != null) return animal.name;
```
